{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01DcaqDAt6L7aVaQiEPWDiyU", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portobelo\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake%27s_Assault_on_Panama\"}, {\"url\": \"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_fortifications_in_America\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://home.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://britannica.com:443/question/How-did-Sir-Francis-Drake-die\"}, {\"url\": \"https://tudorsociety.com/27-january-1596-the-death-of-sir-francis-drake\"}, {\"url\": \"https://mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl/elizabeth\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.heritage-images.com/preview/drakes-funeral-january-1596-c1880-artist-unknown-2648649\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tavistock.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/legacy/meetings/appendices/Agenda%20Item%209%20Appendix%201%20-%20Drakes%20timeline.pdf\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:32:39.318Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Portobelo 1596 Drake died dysentery three forts cannons", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01PBcwWQxvB7oc4aZ9DD1qrU", "content": [{"title": "Portobelo", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portobelo"}, {"title": "Drake%27s Assault on Panama", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Drake%27s_Assault_on_Panama"}, {"title": "Spanish fortifications in America", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spanish_fortifications_in_America"}, {"title": "www.nps.gov", "url": "https://www.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm"}, {"title": "home.nps.gov", "url": "https://home.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm"}, {"title": "How did Sir Francis Drake die?", "url": "https://britannica.com:443/question/How-did-Sir-Francis-Drake-die"}, {"title": "The Tudor Society", "url": "https://tudorsociety.com/27-january-1596-the-death-of-sir-francis-drake"}, {"title": "mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl", "url": "https://mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl/elizabeth"}, {"title": "drakes funeral january 1596 c1880 artist unknown 2648649", "url": "https://www.heritage-images.com/preview/drakes-funeral-january-1596-c1880-artist-unknown-2648649"}, {"title": "Agenda%20Item%209%20Appendix%201%20 %20Drakes%20timeline", "url": "https://www.tavistock.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/legacy/meetings/appendices/Agenda%20Item%209%20Appendix%201%20-%20Drakes%20timeline.pdf"}]}, "The search confirms Drake's death off Portobelo in January 1596, but it returned nothing about three forts or their cannons at Portobelo in that period.\n\n- **Cause and date:** Sources give dysentery as the cause, though one says he died from fever, or possibly dysentery associated with the condition. The date varies: the NPS puts it at January 28, 1596, while the Tudor Society says January 27. A Wikipedia article on Drake's assault gives the night of January 28–29.\n- **Location and burial:** Accounts place his death near Portobelo. The Tudor Society describes a burial at sea in a lead coffin, and the NPS says he was buried at sea near Portobelo.\n- **Fortifications:** The only fortification detail I found is that the Spanish built defensive fortifications at Portobelo to protect it from attacks by other European powers. Nothing I retrieved mentions three forts or their cannon counts for 1596.\n- **Date conflict:** The Portobelo Wikipedia article says the town was founded in 1597, which is inconsistent with Drake's 1596 presence there. This is a source conflict I can't resolve from these results.\n\nTo check the fort and cannon details, I'd need a more specific search, such as one on the Portobelo-San Lorenzo UNESCO fortifications or Spanish colonial coastal defense records from the 1590s."], "durationSeconds": 6.162256875000001, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01DcaqDAt6L7aVaQiEPWDiyU", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
