{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "toolu_01UWmUD9pUiPigdBcZBnYem7", "type": "tool_result", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\"excerpt_removed\": true, \"references\": [{\"url\": \"https://www.mainlesson.com/books/brownee/panama/buccaneers.html\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.heritage-images.com/preview/drakes-funeral-january-1596-c1880-artist-unknown-2648649\"}, {\"url\": \"https://britannica.com:443/question/How-did-Sir-Francis-Drake-die\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://home.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.bloomberg.com/view/articles/2012-05-16/queen-elizabeth-venture-capitalist-for-marauders\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.worldhistory.org/audioplayer/en/2-1867/\"}, {\"url\": \"https://preceden.com/timelines/328286-sir-francis-drake\"}, {\"url\": \"https://mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl/elizabeth\"}, {\"url\": \"https://www.tudorsociety.com/tag/elizabethan-navigators/?amp=1\"}]}"}]}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T00:32:48.431Z", "tool_use_result": {"query": "Portobelo \"tres fuertes\" cañones Drake 1596 disentería", "results": [{"tool_use_id": "srvtoolu_01JusV4CbGGHX3Ac7Ze7VkH1", "content": [{"title": "www.mainlesson.com", "url": "https://www.mainlesson.com/books/brownee/panama/buccaneers.html"}, {"title": "drakes funeral january 1596 c1880 artist unknown 2648649", "url": "https://www.heritage-images.com/preview/drakes-funeral-january-1596-c1880-artist-unknown-2648649"}, {"title": "How did Sir Francis Drake die?", "url": "https://britannica.com:443/question/How-did-Sir-Francis-Drake-die"}, {"title": "www.nps.gov", "url": "https://www.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm"}, {"title": "home.nps.gov", "url": "https://home.nps.gov/people/sirfrancisdrake.htm"}, {"title": "John Steele Gordon, Columnist", "url": "https://www.bloomberg.com/view/articles/2012-05-16/queen-elizabeth-venture-capitalist-for-marauders"}, {"title": "www.worldhistory.org", "url": "https://www.worldhistory.org/audioplayer/en/2-1867/"}, {"title": "328286 sir francis drake", "url": "https://preceden.com/timelines/328286-sir-francis-drake"}, {"title": "mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl", "url": "https://mass.cultureelerfgoed.nl/elizabeth"}, {"title": "elizabethan navigators", "url": "https://www.tudorsociety.com/tag/elizabethan-navigators/?amp=1"}]}, "The search didn't turn up anything about the \"tres fuertes\" fortresses or their cannons. It did confirm the core facts about Drake's death at Portobelo in 1596.\n\n- **Date and cause:** Several sources place Drake's death at Portobelo in late January 1596. One says he died from fever, or possibly dysentery associated with the condition, at sea on January 28, 1596, near Portobelo, Panama. Another dates it to the night of January 28–29 and says Drake died of dysentery aboard his flagship Defiance.\n- **Burial:** He was buried at sea in full armor in a lead-lined coffin.\n- **Illness in the fleet:** One account says the fleet he commanded was decimated by a fever during the final Caribbean voyage.\n- **Wider campaign:** Before his death, the fleet had a few smaller successes attacking towns and fortresses, but disease had sharply reduced its crew. Its attack on Nombre de Dios was repelled, and the English then left.\n- **Shipwrecks:** In 2011 remains of two ships were found by American divers near Portobelo believed to be the Elizabeth and the Delight. The research was done by a Florida museum, and the source notes the British government was not consulted.\n- **Portobelo's defenses:** One source notes that the Spanish Crown invested heavily in defensive fortifications at major treasure ports, though it doesn't name Portobelo's forts or cannons.\n\nNothing I found mentions the \"tres fuertes\" or their cannons, so a search in Spanish on Portobelo's fortifications, such as the San Felipe, Santiago, and San Jerónimo forts, would be needed to cover that part of the query."], "durationSeconds": 6.573682999999999, "searchCount": 1}, "tool_result_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01UWmUD9pUiPigdBcZBnYem7", "permission_decision": {"decision": "accept", "source": "hook", "reason_type": "hook"}}]}
